1
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:05,038
PREVIOUSLY ON CHOSEN HOME

2
00:00:05,105 --> 00:00:06,673
An animal lover
who's gentle-hearted and gay,

3
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:08,074
Genichi Hatano.

4
00:00:08,641 --> 00:00:10,410
The man he fell for

5
00:00:10,477 --> 00:00:11,945
is a gay middle school teacher,

6
00:00:12,012 --> 00:00:12,912
Saku Sakuta.

7
00:00:12,979 --> 00:00:15,181
I broke up with my partner
and ended our cohabitation.

8
00:00:15,248 --> 00:00:16,616
I was spending the night in my car.

9
00:00:16,683 --> 00:00:18,451
What do you think about buying a house?

10
00:00:18,518 --> 00:00:19,986
Could you not come any closer?

11
00:00:20,053 --> 00:00:21,821
The student who gives Saku a headache,

12
00:00:21,888 --> 00:00:23,023
Hotaru Kusunoki,

13
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:25,191
is a 15-year-old Toyoko regular.

14
00:00:25,759 --> 00:00:27,427
That is when…

15
00:00:27,494 --> 00:00:29,329
- What the?
- I'm buying you.

16
00:00:29,396 --> 00:00:30,630
Parent-Child Contract.

17
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:32,399
I need someone to pretend to be my parent.

18
00:00:33,366 --> 00:00:35,035
Party A’s mother, Tomoe Kusunoki,

19
00:00:35,101 --> 00:00:38,004
is wanted for embezzlement
from her company and is on the run.

20
00:00:38,905 --> 00:00:40,006
Since then, I’ve been on my own.

21
00:00:40,073 --> 00:00:42,709
After hearing Hotaru's story,

22
00:00:42,776 --> 00:00:44,844
Genichi decides to pose as her dad.

23
00:00:44,911 --> 00:00:45,812
I'm Jin Ichigaya.

24
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:47,347
Meanwhile, her actual dad…

25
00:00:47,414 --> 00:00:48,748
Did Mom call you?

26
00:00:49,616 --> 00:00:52,719
…seems to be plotting something.

27
00:00:52,786 --> 00:00:55,021
I left a suitcase.

28
00:00:55,088 --> 00:00:58,091
What’s inside belongs to us.

29
00:00:58,591 --> 00:01:00,060
I’m leaving it in your care.

30
00:01:00,126 --> 00:01:01,294
I'll be back.

31
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:04,431
Thank you.

32
00:01:04,497 --> 00:01:05,565
TAMOTSU’S LITTLE GIFT SHOP

33
00:01:05,632 --> 00:01:06,566
DIRECT PEACH DELIVERY AVAILABLE

34
00:01:10,103 --> 00:01:11,271
Hi.

35
00:01:11,337 --> 00:01:12,272
FUKUSHIMA

36
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:14,941
Bye.

37
00:01:20,346 --> 00:01:21,614
TOMOE KUSUNOKI

38
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:25,518
Off you go.

39
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,701
Good morning.

40
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:43,103
Morning.

41
00:01:43,169 --> 00:01:45,972
I made too much breakfast.

42
00:01:46,039 --> 00:01:47,173
I always skip breakfast.

43
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:49,442
I've got salmon, seaweed, kelp,

44
00:01:49,509 --> 00:01:51,044
- sesame and salt.
- Listen.

45
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:52,946
- Pick whichever--
- I'm good.

46
00:01:53,012 --> 00:01:54,581
Oh, by any chance,

47
00:01:54,647 --> 00:01:57,684
are you one of those people
who can’t eat food made by others?

48
00:01:57,750 --> 00:01:59,219
That's not it.

49
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:00,854
You can rest assured.

50
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,323
I wrapped them in cling film
before shaping them.

51
00:02:03,389 --> 00:02:04,524
As I said,

52
00:02:05,391 --> 00:02:07,627
- I don’t need any!
- Oh, I get it.

53
00:02:08,228 --> 00:02:09,562
You wouldn't want anything

54
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:11,865
from an old guy like me.

55
00:02:11,931 --> 00:02:12,699
Right?

56
00:02:15,201 --> 00:02:16,169
May I have kelp, please?

57
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:17,203
No need to force--

58
00:02:17,270 --> 00:02:18,138
One kelp, please!

59
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:22,442
- I'm starting to get hungry.
- Is that right?

60
00:02:22,509 --> 00:02:23,610
Then, here's your kelp.

61
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:30,183
You really don’t have to mind me.
Once I find a place, I’ll move out.

62
00:02:31,284 --> 00:02:34,120
If you want, I can introduce you
to a property agent.

63
00:02:34,187 --> 00:02:36,689
I've got a friend who works as one.

64
00:02:36,756 --> 00:02:39,159
- I'm sure he'll help you out.
- Oh, shoot!

65
00:02:39,225 --> 00:02:41,494
Sorry, I'm running late.

66
00:02:41,561 --> 00:02:42,529
Okay.

67
00:02:42,595 --> 00:02:43,429
Sorry about this.

68
00:02:43,496 --> 00:02:44,764
We're leaving.

69
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:45,932
Drive safely.

70
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:51,771
‪INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

71
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:52,739
Good morning.

72
00:02:52,805 --> 00:02:53,806
Good morning.

73
00:02:53,873 --> 00:02:55,341
- Pick one you like.
- Hm?

74
00:02:55,408 --> 00:02:56,276
Your breakfast.

75
00:02:56,342 --> 00:02:57,277
I'm fine with any.

76
00:02:57,944 --> 00:02:59,546
That's the hardest to work with.

77
00:02:59,612 --> 00:03:01,147
- Pick one--
- Salmon!

78
00:03:01,214 --> 00:03:02,749
Okay. Good morning.

79
00:03:02,815 --> 00:03:04,617
- Good morning.
- Morning.

80
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:05,552
Go ahead.

81
00:03:06,119 --> 00:03:07,720
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

82
00:03:07,787 --> 00:03:09,455
Thank you!

83
00:03:11,424 --> 00:03:12,559
What's that?

84
00:03:13,493 --> 00:03:15,094
Scavengers have been appearing lately.

85
00:03:15,161 --> 00:03:16,930
They’re probably just hungry,

86
00:03:16,996 --> 00:03:18,998
so I put this here to keep the crows away.

87
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:21,935
Both of you should get going!

88
00:03:22,001 --> 00:03:23,136
- See you.
- See you.

89
00:03:23,203 --> 00:03:24,170
Let's go.

90
00:03:25,471 --> 00:03:26,773
You can eat at least two, yes?

91
00:03:30,743 --> 00:03:33,012
You only need to act like my dad
when I ask you to.

92
00:03:33,079 --> 00:03:33,913
Huh?

93
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:35,715
Please don't get too involved.

94
00:03:36,249 --> 00:03:37,150
Bye.

95
00:03:42,455 --> 00:03:45,825
But make sure you don't expose yourself
in front of my teacher!

96
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:46,893
Keep up the parent act.

97
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:49,395
Right, got it.

98
00:04:05,678 --> 00:04:07,180
Keep up the act?

99
00:04:21,494 --> 00:04:23,963
‪INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

100
00:04:33,306 --> 00:04:35,208
- How may I help you?
- Huh?

101
00:04:35,275 --> 00:04:36,509
I'm the landlady.

102
00:04:38,511 --> 00:04:39,712
Please pardon my rudeness.

103
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:42,181
I'll come back later.

104
00:04:55,061 --> 00:04:57,230
Embezzlement of 30 million yen?

105
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:59,832
A female employee is currently on the run.

106
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:02,201
On the second of this month,

107
00:05:02,268 --> 00:05:04,370
in a company located in Suginami, Tokyo,

108
00:05:04,437 --> 00:05:06,005
around 30 million yen

109
00:05:06,072 --> 00:05:08,675
was discovered missing.

110
00:05:08,741 --> 00:05:10,343
- Old news, huh?
- It was found that employee

111
00:05:10,410 --> 00:05:12,078
- What?
- Tomoe Kusunoki, age 43…

112
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:14,247
- I knew it. I've seen it before.
- Hey!

113
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:15,948
It was in the news a while back.

114
00:05:16,015 --> 00:05:18,751
- Thirty million, eh? How nice.
- Police say the suspect, Kusunoki,

115
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:22,455
has been missing
since the case came to light.

116
00:05:25,792 --> 00:05:26,793
Hi.

117
00:05:26,859 --> 00:05:29,062
- Thanks for looking after my daughter.
- Hey!

118
00:05:35,368 --> 00:05:37,403
I knew you looked familiar!

119
00:05:37,470 --> 00:05:38,538
What do you want?

120
00:05:39,372 --> 00:05:41,441
Did you make up with him?

121
00:05:41,507 --> 00:05:42,608
Who are you referring to?

122
00:05:42,675 --> 00:05:44,110
Oh, come on now!

123
00:05:44,744 --> 00:05:46,412
You were with him at the crepe place.

124
00:05:46,479 --> 00:05:49,716
I’ve never eaten a crepe before.

125
00:05:51,050 --> 00:05:52,518
That’s a bit hard to believe.

126
00:05:52,585 --> 00:05:53,986
If you’ll excuse me.

127
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:58,157
REAL ESTATE SITE

128
00:05:58,224 --> 00:05:59,125
Are you moving?

129
00:05:59,992 --> 00:06:01,494
- Huh?
- With your girlfriend.

130
00:06:02,562 --> 00:06:04,263
It's only for me.

131
00:06:04,864 --> 00:06:06,232
Really, man?

132
00:06:06,299 --> 00:06:09,202
You’re eating a homemade rice ball,
so I thought you got a girlfriend.

133
00:06:09,268 --> 00:06:11,070
Plus, you're browsing apartments,

134
00:06:11,137 --> 00:06:12,572
so I was convinced that you and her--

135
00:06:12,638 --> 00:06:13,973
You couldn't be more wrong!

136
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,241
Mr. Sakuta.

137
00:06:15,775 --> 00:06:17,877
Oh, hold on.

138
00:06:20,913 --> 00:06:21,748
Here.

139
00:06:22,281 --> 00:06:24,417
When will you find something
that you like?

140
00:06:24,484 --> 00:06:25,651
OTHER CAREER PATH
FIND SOMETHING I LOVE

141
00:06:25,718 --> 00:06:26,652
No idea.

142
00:06:26,719 --> 00:06:27,920
Nothing comes to mind at all?

143
00:06:29,522 --> 00:06:31,224
If I had to name one, it'd be miso soup.

144
00:06:31,290 --> 00:06:32,392
And shishamo.

145
00:06:32,458 --> 00:06:34,360
I'm not asking about what you like to eat.

146
00:06:34,427 --> 00:06:35,261
Then, I'm out of ideas.

147
00:06:35,328 --> 00:06:37,497
You could start with the things you like

148
00:06:37,563 --> 00:06:39,165
or with the high school you want to go to.

149
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:41,067
High school?

150
00:06:41,134 --> 00:06:42,635
- You're going, right?
- Probably.

151
00:06:42,702 --> 00:06:44,704
List a few schools that interest you
and resubmit it.

152
00:06:44,771 --> 00:06:47,006
If you’re unsure, you can ask
your dad or me.

153
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:48,307
Feel free to consult, yeah?

154
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:51,577
Thank you.

155
00:06:55,181 --> 00:06:56,349
CAREER PATH GUIDANCE

156
00:06:59,652 --> 00:07:01,554
I have this one.
I always put it on my bag.

157
00:07:01,621 --> 00:07:02,522
What are you doing?

158
00:07:03,122 --> 00:07:06,292
We've got some leftover keychains
from organizing the shop’s stock.

159
00:07:06,359 --> 00:07:08,261
Mr. Hatano, if there’s anything you want…

160
00:07:08,327 --> 00:07:09,328
Are you sure it's okay?

161
00:07:10,363 --> 00:07:11,664
Oh, wow.

162
00:07:11,731 --> 00:07:12,598
What's this?

163
00:07:13,533 --> 00:07:15,301
- A bird?
- Nah.

164
00:07:15,368 --> 00:07:16,269
Really?

165
00:07:16,335 --> 00:07:17,570
Look, it has four legs.

166
00:07:17,637 --> 00:07:18,671
Oh, you're right.

167
00:07:18,738 --> 00:07:20,239
Then, what is it?

168
00:07:20,306 --> 00:07:22,175
But it's kinda cute.

169
00:07:22,909 --> 00:07:24,277
It seems to be smiling too.

170
00:07:24,977 --> 00:07:26,646
Doesn't it look angry though?

171
00:07:26,712 --> 00:07:27,680
No, it's crying.

172
00:07:29,682 --> 00:07:34,487
Walk, walk, a little walk

173
00:07:34,554 --> 00:07:38,624
Angry? Sad?

174
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:40,359
Wanna have a water break?

175
00:07:40,426 --> 00:07:41,260
Okay.

176
00:07:42,562 --> 00:07:43,830
Here you go.

177
00:07:45,097 --> 00:07:46,732
Walk…

178
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,268
- Do you need a receipt?
- Nope.

179
00:07:49,335 --> 00:07:51,137
Thank you.

180
00:07:51,204 --> 00:07:53,906
- Welcome.
- Here.

181
00:08:00,546 --> 00:08:02,715
Do you have something to prove your age?

182
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:05,418
I don’t have it with me right now.

183
00:08:06,085 --> 00:08:06,919
Deadass,

184
00:08:06,986 --> 00:08:08,754
I thought I could pull it off!

185
00:08:08,821 --> 00:08:09,922
Weirdly confident.

186
00:08:09,989 --> 00:08:11,557
Anyone can tell you're a minor.

187
00:08:11,624 --> 00:08:13,793
You should've told me before I queued up!

188
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:14,760
Oh, Bayashiko!

189
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:16,095
- Yo!
- What's up!

190
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:17,697
What are you all doing?

191
00:08:17,763 --> 00:08:19,532
A game. Have a look!

192
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:22,235
That cashier is crazy with the age checks.

193
00:08:22,301 --> 00:08:24,370
No matter how adult-like you act,
you can’t get past him.

194
00:08:24,437 --> 00:08:26,205
Apparently, no one has ever succeeded.

195
00:08:26,272 --> 00:08:28,975
So, we're trying to see
who's able to succeed first.

196
00:08:29,041 --> 00:08:31,844
- Huh? What a dumb game!
- Thank you.

197
00:08:31,911 --> 00:08:33,112
What about that guy?

198
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:36,849
- No way he's a teen.
- Do you have something to prove your age?

199
00:08:36,916 --> 00:08:38,351
He's got to be an uncle.

200
00:08:38,417 --> 00:08:39,619
I'm clearly an adult.

201
00:08:39,685 --> 00:08:41,420
He looks every bit an old man.

202
00:08:43,289 --> 00:08:44,790
Sorry, sir,

203
00:08:44,857 --> 00:08:47,393
you’re under 20,
so I can’t sell you alcohol.

204
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:49,695
- What? He's a minor?
- How did he know?

205
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:52,665
This is going to be a tough battle.

206
00:08:53,232 --> 00:08:54,834
We just gotta act like an adult, right?

207
00:08:55,501 --> 00:08:57,069
Like, worry about health exam results.

208
00:08:57,136 --> 00:08:58,371
Or raise our voices on the phone.

209
00:08:58,437 --> 00:09:00,172
Or talk endlessly about our younger days!

210
00:09:00,239 --> 00:09:01,707
That's it!

211
00:09:01,774 --> 00:09:03,209
What are you all up to?

212
00:09:04,343 --> 00:09:05,778
- Or grow a beard.
- What?

213
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:09,048
In any case, it's getting late.

214
00:09:09,115 --> 00:09:09,949
Or being a busybody.

215
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:12,685
Oh, this is such a stupid game!

216
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:14,253
What's going on?

217
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:17,657
REAL ESTATE SITE

218
00:09:18,724 --> 00:09:19,625
Good evening.

219
00:09:20,192 --> 00:09:21,861
Sorry for intruding.

220
00:09:21,928 --> 00:09:24,297
Oh, not at all.
Please make yourself at home.

221
00:09:24,363 --> 00:09:25,998
Not that I have any right to say so.

222
00:09:29,335 --> 00:09:31,404
It was delicious. The rice ball, I meant.

223
00:09:32,538 --> 00:09:33,606
That's great to hear!

224
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:43,783
Sorry, but about my daughter…

225
00:09:45,685 --> 00:09:47,053
What about her?

226
00:09:47,119 --> 00:09:49,322
How much do you know about her mom's case?

227
00:09:49,388 --> 00:09:52,224
Nothing beyond what’s in the news.

228
00:09:52,959 --> 00:09:53,793
Right.

229
00:09:53,859 --> 00:09:55,861
Did they not ask you for any details?

230
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:58,230
The police, I mean.
Since you’re her ex-husband.

231
00:09:59,699 --> 00:10:00,800
Well…

232
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:03,035
REAL ESTATE SITE

233
00:10:05,004 --> 00:10:08,007
About the property agent
I told you this morning…

234
00:10:08,074 --> 00:10:09,475
I'm good, really.

235
00:10:09,542 --> 00:10:11,010
But…

236
00:10:11,077 --> 00:10:13,446
I’ve been depending on you a bit too much.

237
00:10:13,512 --> 00:10:16,148
I feel this isn’t really appropriate.

238
00:10:16,215 --> 00:10:17,750
After all, we're teacher and parent.

239
00:10:17,817 --> 00:10:19,218
But that property agent…

240
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:20,419
Didn't you hear what I said?

241
00:10:21,220 --> 00:10:23,356
Distance. Keep your distance.

242
00:10:23,422 --> 00:10:25,858
But this is really for your sake, Sakuta.

243
00:10:25,925 --> 00:10:27,293
What does that mean?

244
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:29,261
He’s really a great guy.

245
00:10:29,328 --> 00:10:30,363
He even takes guys

246
00:10:30,429 --> 00:10:33,733
like us into account
when looking for a place.

247
00:10:34,767 --> 00:10:35,768
I'm good.

248
00:10:37,503 --> 00:10:39,005
You’ve already got a place in mind?

249
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:42,708
Not… yet.

250
00:10:43,509 --> 00:10:44,677
Then…

251
00:10:45,945 --> 00:10:46,946
Okay?

252
00:10:48,447 --> 00:10:49,749
Very well.

253
00:10:50,416 --> 00:10:52,184
- Please go ahead with it.
- Alright.

254
00:10:53,919 --> 00:10:55,021
See you.

255
00:10:55,821 --> 00:10:56,656
I'm home, Dad!

256
00:10:56,722 --> 00:10:58,157
Oh, welcome home.

257
00:10:58,224 --> 00:10:59,225
You're late.

258
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:02,395
Good night.

259
00:11:05,765 --> 00:11:06,832
Good night…

260
00:11:10,469 --> 00:11:11,504
Good night!

261
00:11:13,939 --> 00:11:15,808
I met your dad today.

262
00:11:15,875 --> 00:11:17,643
The real one.

263
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:18,544
Where?

264
00:11:19,111 --> 00:11:20,246
The park.

265
00:11:20,312 --> 00:11:21,414
It was purely coincidence.

266
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,581
Did you guys talk?

267
00:11:22,648 --> 00:11:23,749
Not much.

268
00:11:23,816 --> 00:11:26,652
We just talked about the time
at the crepe place, and that's about it.

269
00:11:29,655 --> 00:11:31,323
You'll still be here for a while, right?

270
00:11:31,891 --> 00:11:32,758
Yes.

271
00:11:33,626 --> 00:11:35,327
Until my teacher sleeps.

272
00:11:37,329 --> 00:11:39,565
Okay then, let's have dinner.

273
00:11:40,633 --> 00:11:42,134
Here you go.

274
00:11:45,137 --> 00:11:46,672
What do you usually eat?

275
00:11:46,739 --> 00:11:50,776
Discounted supermarket bento.

276
00:11:50,843 --> 00:11:53,179
And sometimes I make miso soup myself.

277
00:11:54,213 --> 00:11:57,216
Really? Okay, let's eat. Have a seat.

278
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:02,154
Let's dig in!

279
00:12:03,289 --> 00:12:04,657
Thank you…

280
00:12:13,332 --> 00:12:14,567
What, it doesn't taste good?

281
00:12:15,367 --> 00:12:16,235
No…

282
00:12:16,769 --> 00:12:18,337
It just tastes different.

283
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:19,305
What do you mean?

284
00:12:19,972 --> 00:12:20,806
From my mom's.

285
00:12:21,507 --> 00:12:22,341
How does hers taste?

286
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:24,443
- She had a secret ingredient.
- Yeah?

287
00:12:24,510 --> 00:12:25,611
And it makes the soup mild.

288
00:12:25,678 --> 00:12:28,781
I see. What's the secret ingredient?

289
00:12:29,882 --> 00:12:31,350
- A secret.
- Figured.

290
00:12:32,952 --> 00:12:35,755
- What kind of person was your mom?
- Hm?

291
00:12:35,821 --> 00:12:38,357
Well, you know… It’d be weird
not to know, right?

292
00:12:38,924 --> 00:12:41,427
Like her hobbies, personality, quirks…

293
00:12:43,362 --> 00:12:45,331
- Are they similar to yours?
- Not at all.

294
00:12:45,397 --> 00:12:46,532
Be it looks or personality.

295
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:47,666
Is that so?

296
00:12:50,703 --> 00:12:52,938
She just seemed like someone
who works really hard.

297
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:55,441
She was doing her best

298
00:12:55,508 --> 00:12:57,042
at lots of things, I think.

299
00:12:57,109 --> 00:12:58,978
Then both of you are similar.

300
00:13:04,049 --> 00:13:05,151
I don't know.

301
00:13:06,852 --> 00:13:08,220
HIBINO REAL ESTATE

302
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:09,388
Wait, wait… Huh?

303
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:11,857
You’re going to pretend to be
that Kusunoki girl's parent

304
00:13:11,924 --> 00:13:14,693
and her homeroom teacher
is on his way now? Huh?

305
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:16,929
Sorry for dragging you into this.

306
00:13:16,996 --> 00:13:18,898
- This is entertaining!
- What?

307
00:13:18,964 --> 00:13:20,065
Leave it to me.

308
00:13:20,132 --> 00:13:21,167
I’ll help with anything.

309
00:13:22,434 --> 00:13:24,770
Also, I’m supposed to go by my stage name.

310
00:13:24,837 --> 00:13:26,071
What stage name?

311
00:13:26,138 --> 00:13:28,507
When I was aiming to be a musician…
Go along with it, okay?

312
00:13:28,574 --> 00:13:30,276
Stage name…?

313
00:13:30,342 --> 00:13:31,277
Welcome!

314
00:13:32,378 --> 00:13:33,445
Over here.

315
00:13:34,079 --> 00:13:35,748
Hello. Nice to meet you.

316
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:37,049
Nice to meet you.

317
00:13:37,750 --> 00:13:39,552
I’m from Hibino Real Estate…

318
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:41,487
and my name is Okabe.

319
00:13:42,988 --> 00:13:44,089
I'm Sakuta.

320
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:46,292
- Pleased to meet you.
- Same here.

321
00:13:46,358 --> 00:13:47,226
Have a seat.

322
00:13:47,293 --> 00:13:48,127
- Here.
- Thank you.

323
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:50,496
Some water too.

324
00:13:52,097 --> 00:13:53,499
He roughly knows the situation.

325
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:58,003
You're Kusunoki's homeroom teacher, right?

326
00:13:58,070 --> 00:13:59,138
Yes.

327
00:13:59,205 --> 00:14:02,274
And I'm borrowing the yard
at Inokashira Apartments.

328
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:03,609
Sorry for the late notification.

329
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:06,779
No issues. As long as you’ve spoken
with the landlady,

330
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:07,947
we’re fine.

331
00:14:08,013 --> 00:14:09,582
- Thank you.
- Don't worry about it.

332
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:16,689
Were both of you classmates
or something like that?

333
00:14:16,755 --> 00:14:17,923
Oh, no.

334
00:14:17,990 --> 00:14:20,893
It started when Genichi
was busking at the station…

335
00:14:21,594 --> 00:14:23,329
So, people do call him by his stage name!

336
00:14:24,063 --> 00:14:25,064
Pardon?

337
00:14:26,098 --> 00:14:28,767
Yeah! Of course!

338
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:32,671
Right. His stage name…

339
00:14:33,339 --> 00:14:34,406
Genichi.

340
00:14:37,009 --> 00:14:38,477
Well then, let's get started right away.

341
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:39,745
Right.

342
00:14:39,812 --> 00:14:42,514
Let’s start by hearing your requirements.

343
00:14:43,515 --> 00:14:44,483
Okay.

344
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:46,886
‪Please give me a moment.

345
00:14:50,089 --> 00:14:50,923
Um…

346
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:53,292
I'm fine by myself from here on.

347
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:55,261
Just in case, you know…

348
00:14:55,327 --> 00:14:57,596
NARIWADAI HIGH SCHOOL

349
00:14:59,531 --> 00:15:00,499
TRUE MIRIN

350
00:15:08,941 --> 00:15:10,276
BAYASHIKO IS TRYING
TO BYPASS THE AGE-CHECK TODAY!

351
00:15:10,342 --> 00:15:11,844
ALL TO GATHER AT THE CONVENIENCE STORE!

352
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:19,118
- You scared me!
- My bad.

353
00:15:19,184 --> 00:15:20,419
What is it?

354
00:15:20,486 --> 00:15:21,687
The other day,

355
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:25,457
some middle-aged man came by.

356
00:15:25,524 --> 00:15:26,358
A man?

357
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:27,826
I don't know how to put it,

358
00:15:27,893 --> 00:15:28,928
but he had a shady vibe.

359
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:34,533
- What's that?
- I'll leave this with you.

360
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,335
Use this when things go south.

361
00:15:36,402 --> 00:15:37,303
- Huh?
- Take it.

362
00:15:38,904 --> 00:15:40,406
Restrain him like this, okay?

363
00:15:40,472 --> 00:15:41,307
Hey, wait!

364
00:15:47,913 --> 00:15:50,349
DAD

365
00:15:53,519 --> 00:15:56,989
Based on your requirements,

366
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:59,291
it’d be these few apartments.

367
00:15:59,358 --> 00:16:00,559
Thank you.

368
00:16:00,626 --> 00:16:01,994
Oh?

369
00:16:02,061 --> 00:16:04,596
Is there any place that catches your eye?

370
00:16:04,663 --> 00:16:06,632
Let me see…

371
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:08,133
This one, maybe.

372
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,635
I'm not asking you, Genichi.

373
00:16:09,702 --> 00:16:10,602
Right.

374
00:16:10,669 --> 00:16:14,573
Is there a place where I wouldn’t
have to run into the other residents?

375
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:15,507
Huh?

376
00:16:15,574 --> 00:16:17,810
I don’t really like people prying
into my business.

377
00:16:17,876 --> 00:16:19,778
Oh, okay.

378
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:22,948
Is he aware of that?

379
00:16:23,015 --> 00:16:24,183
No. I'll leave that to you.

380
00:16:25,884 --> 00:16:27,553
Well, uh…

381
00:16:27,619 --> 00:16:28,821
I'm gay as well.

382
00:16:30,055 --> 00:16:31,256
Is that so?

383
00:16:31,857 --> 00:16:33,859
So, you’d prefer to avoid seeing people?

384
00:16:33,926 --> 00:16:35,327
At my previous place,

385
00:16:35,394 --> 00:16:37,763
I lived with my partner.

386
00:16:38,297 --> 00:16:41,133
People stared at us a lot
when we were together.

387
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:43,402
This time, I’m living alone,

388
00:16:43,469 --> 00:16:45,404
so it’s fine as long as I’m careful.

389
00:16:46,105 --> 00:16:48,207
I just thought I’d mention it,

390
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:51,677
since I heard
you’re understanding about it.

391
00:16:52,311 --> 00:16:53,812
I’m sure you already know,

392
00:16:53,879 --> 00:16:56,682
but these days, some properties
call themselves LGBTQ-friendly,

393
00:16:56,749 --> 00:16:59,651
and they don't discriminate
based on sexuality.

394
00:16:59,718 --> 00:17:01,487
There are a few places like that around.

395
00:17:01,553 --> 00:17:03,255
With your requirements however,

396
00:17:03,322 --> 00:17:05,791
there aren’t really any
I can recommend at the moment.

397
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:07,659
Based on what I've heard, though,

398
00:17:07,726 --> 00:17:10,262
the places that don’t seem discriminatory

399
00:17:10,329 --> 00:17:14,066
and seem like comfortable environments
are this… and this.

400
00:17:14,133 --> 00:17:16,735
What do you think?
Any you’d like to go see?

401
00:17:17,436 --> 00:17:19,371
Let me think.

402
00:17:20,005 --> 00:17:21,607
Hey, does this have rooftop access?

403
00:17:21,673 --> 00:17:24,209
Oh, yes. There's no balcony,
but in place of that…

404
00:17:24,276 --> 00:17:27,179
Airing out the futon there
would feel so nice.

405
00:17:27,246 --> 00:17:28,480
You could even stargaze, right?

406
00:17:28,547 --> 00:17:30,816
Oh, that’s so nice. Don't you think so?

407
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:32,051
This one too!

408
00:17:32,117 --> 00:17:33,752
You seem to be enjoying yourself.

409
00:17:34,319 --> 00:17:36,989
Sorry, I got too carried away.

410
00:17:39,024 --> 00:17:41,794
Let’s check this one out
for the time being.

411
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:44,229
Very well. Please wait a moment.

412
00:17:46,565 --> 00:17:48,167
Your previous place

413
00:17:48,901 --> 00:17:50,469
was where you lived with Yoshida?

414
00:17:50,536 --> 00:17:51,703
That's right.

415
00:17:51,770 --> 00:17:53,705
He might still be living there alone.

416
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:55,641
How are things since then?

417
00:17:56,475 --> 00:17:57,443
What do you mean?

418
00:17:58,444 --> 00:18:00,546
Well, between you and Yoshida.

419
00:18:01,213 --> 00:18:04,283
- Nothing happened, unfortunately.
- Unfortunately?

420
00:18:04,349 --> 00:18:06,185
You were hoping
we'd get back together, no?

421
00:18:06,852 --> 00:18:10,355
Oh, no. You shouldn't get back together.
Just let things move forward as they are.

422
00:18:11,723 --> 00:18:12,658
Huh?

423
00:18:12,724 --> 00:18:15,127
We're able to do a viewing this weekend.
Does that work?

424
00:18:16,061 --> 00:18:17,863
Hold on…

425
00:18:18,964 --> 00:18:20,299
This weekend…

426
00:18:21,066 --> 00:18:22,067
This weekend works.

427
00:18:24,169 --> 00:18:25,304
Huh?

428
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:26,772
What?

429
00:18:26,839 --> 00:18:28,440
How was the parent-teacher meeting?

430
00:18:28,507 --> 00:18:30,876
Have you decided on your path?

431
00:18:34,379 --> 00:18:35,647
Are you studying hard for exams?

432
00:18:35,714 --> 00:18:38,250
Didn't I say not to interfere?
What's with you?

433
00:18:38,851 --> 00:18:40,519
No, you didn't.

434
00:18:40,586 --> 00:18:42,521
Please stop coming to my apartment too.

435
00:18:42,588 --> 00:18:44,256
450 YEN FOR CREPE

436
00:18:44,323 --> 00:18:45,190
You came, didn't you?

437
00:18:49,661 --> 00:18:50,829
The 30 million yen.

438
00:18:51,763 --> 00:18:52,731
Where did you hide it?

439
00:18:53,465 --> 00:18:55,567
You must know something, right?

440
00:18:56,168 --> 00:18:57,035
No, I don't.

441
00:18:57,102 --> 00:19:00,105
But it’s weird
that it hasn’t been found yet.

442
00:19:00,172 --> 00:19:01,673
Mom must've taken it and ran off.

443
00:19:01,740 --> 00:19:03,909
Or she may have hidden it somewhere.

444
00:19:06,912 --> 00:19:08,647
- Let me in your unit.
- Hell no.

445
00:19:08,714 --> 00:19:10,616
I just need some cash.

446
00:19:11,350 --> 00:19:13,352
The police already searched
the entire place.

447
00:19:13,418 --> 00:19:16,221
Then what’s the problem?
I just want to check for myself.

448
00:19:16,288 --> 00:19:19,124
I just don’t like strangers
going inside my house.

449
00:19:19,725 --> 00:19:21,293
What stranger?

450
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:23,662
You stopped being my dad, didn’t you?

451
00:19:25,497 --> 00:19:29,334
I still think of myself as your dad.

452
00:19:29,401 --> 00:19:30,569
Oh, shut up.

453
00:19:30,636 --> 00:19:32,971
Stop contacting me too.

454
00:19:44,049 --> 00:19:46,718
Thank you. Welcome.

455
00:19:46,785 --> 00:19:48,487
Here.

456
00:19:48,554 --> 00:19:49,688
Will it work?

457
00:19:57,629 --> 00:19:59,865
Do you have something to prove your age?

458
00:20:00,632 --> 00:20:02,100
I forgot to bring it with me.

459
00:20:02,167 --> 00:20:04,136
That totally failed, huh?

460
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:07,206
Hey, Hotaru?

461
00:20:12,077 --> 00:20:12,945
What's wrong?

462
00:20:13,679 --> 00:20:14,980
- I'm buying this.
- Huh?

463
00:20:16,315 --> 00:20:18,217
- Welcome.
- Here.

464
00:20:18,283 --> 00:20:19,384
‪TRUE ‪MIRIN

465
00:20:20,118 --> 00:20:22,054
Do you have something to prove your age?

466
00:20:23,155 --> 00:20:26,558
True mirin contains alcohol,
so it can’t be sold to anyone under 20.

467
00:20:27,459 --> 00:20:28,293
No way.

468
00:20:28,927 --> 00:20:31,263
SAKUTA'S HOUSE VIEWING DATE

469
00:20:36,134 --> 00:20:37,502
Sock?

470
00:20:37,569 --> 00:20:40,572
Yeah. It fell behind the washing machine.
The Santa-patterned one.

471
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:44,509
Also, your mail is still coming here.

472
00:20:45,010 --> 00:20:46,311
Haven’t you set up forwarding?

473
00:20:46,878 --> 00:20:49,514
- Nope.
- I'll send them to you. Where do you live?

474
00:20:50,082 --> 00:20:51,183
I've got no address.

475
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,452
- Huh?
- I’m sleeping in my car.

476
00:20:53,952 --> 00:20:55,254
You what?

477
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:56,521
Yeah.

478
00:20:56,588 --> 00:20:59,758
But it’s been two to three months
since you left.

479
00:21:00,325 --> 00:21:02,094
I’ll let you know when I find a place!

480
00:21:03,328 --> 00:21:04,563
Okay.

481
00:21:04,630 --> 00:21:05,464
Well then.

482
00:21:05,530 --> 00:21:07,332
SAKUTA

483
00:21:15,474 --> 00:21:16,341
Was this on purpose?

484
00:21:26,618 --> 00:21:28,620
Do you live in this apartment?

485
00:21:28,687 --> 00:21:29,821
Yeah, I guess.

486
00:21:29,888 --> 00:21:32,591
Do you know who lives
in the second-floor apartment?

487
00:21:32,658 --> 00:21:33,558
Or when they'll be back?

488
00:21:34,693 --> 00:21:36,194
Not really.

489
00:21:36,261 --> 00:21:37,095
I see.

490
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:42,067
- Ran away from home?
- What?

491
00:21:43,035 --> 00:21:46,571
I get it. I really do.
Guys don’t have a place at home.

492
00:21:46,638 --> 00:21:48,840
That’s when you just retreat to the car.

493
00:21:50,809 --> 00:21:51,677
Well…

494
00:21:51,743 --> 00:21:53,812
Anyway, I’ll just be there waiting.

495
00:21:59,618 --> 00:22:01,853
- I can’t wait to be an adult!
- I know!

496
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,588
I can then buy true mirin.

497
00:22:03,655 --> 00:22:05,524
You really wanted that?

498
00:22:06,058 --> 00:22:07,292
What’ll you do first as an adult?

499
00:22:07,359 --> 00:22:08,260
Drink alcohol.

500
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:09,328
Seriously?

501
00:22:09,828 --> 00:22:11,763
I'M WAITING AT YOUR APARTMENT - DAD

502
00:22:14,766 --> 00:22:15,634
What's wrong?

503
00:22:18,270 --> 00:22:19,137
It's nothing.

504
00:22:55,073 --> 00:22:57,175
Ouch…

505
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:01,613
It's me.

506
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:02,647
Coming.

507
00:23:03,815 --> 00:23:05,384
- Good morning.
- I'm back.

508
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:07,853
You just came back?

509
00:23:07,919 --> 00:23:09,821
Mr. Sakuta has already woken up.

510
00:23:10,489 --> 00:23:12,724
Hey, where were you?

511
00:23:14,393 --> 00:23:15,460
Toyoko?

512
00:23:16,061 --> 00:23:18,430
Is everything okay?
Isn't that place dangerous?

513
00:23:18,997 --> 00:23:20,165
I never asked.

514
00:23:20,866 --> 00:23:23,301
I never asked you to worry
or make me meals.

515
00:23:23,368 --> 00:23:25,270
Stop acting on your own and getting mad.

516
00:23:25,904 --> 00:23:27,506
What?

517
00:23:29,074 --> 00:23:31,410
Did any suspicious person come by?

518
00:23:32,310 --> 00:23:33,245
Suspicious person?

519
00:23:33,945 --> 00:23:35,180
Never mind.

520
00:23:36,148 --> 00:23:37,849
I’ll head back to my room soon.

521
00:23:44,856 --> 00:23:47,058
UNIFORM

522
00:23:49,327 --> 00:23:51,797
TOMOE KUSUNOKI EMBEZZLEMENT WITNESS

523
00:23:51,863 --> 00:23:54,065
NO RESULTS FOUND FOR THOSE KEYWORDS

524
00:23:59,938 --> 00:24:02,774
- Sakuta.
- Yes?

525
00:24:04,176 --> 00:24:06,511
Being a parent… It’s hard.

526
00:24:07,078 --> 00:24:09,014
Whether I make her meals
or worry about her,

527
00:24:10,148 --> 00:24:12,050
she said it’s none of my business.

528
00:24:12,117 --> 00:24:15,654
Oh, that’s exactly what I imagined.

529
00:24:16,555 --> 00:24:17,689
What?

530
00:24:17,756 --> 00:24:18,824
Of a parent-child fight.

531
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:23,462
‪Really?

532
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:27,732
Ah, sorry for the wait.
I’ll unlock it now.

533
00:24:27,799 --> 00:24:28,733
Thank you.

534
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:30,769
- Nice to meet you.
- Likewise.

535
00:24:32,003 --> 00:24:33,238
Are you siblings?

536
00:24:34,172 --> 00:24:36,341
- No.
- Friends?

537
00:24:36,408 --> 00:24:38,577
Two people might find it a bit small.

538
00:24:38,643 --> 00:24:40,512
Oh, no. I’m just accompanying him.

539
00:24:41,079 --> 00:24:43,181
This is Mr. Sakuta,
the one interested in the unit.

540
00:24:43,248 --> 00:24:44,716
Oh, sorry about that.

541
00:24:44,783 --> 00:24:46,184
Feel free to look around.

542
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:48,653
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

543
00:24:49,287 --> 00:24:52,123
It’s about 30 square meters.

544
00:24:53,425 --> 00:24:55,560
It’s an old place,

545
00:24:55,627 --> 00:24:57,329
but it’s been renovated a few times,

546
00:24:57,963 --> 00:24:59,631
so the bath and kitchen areas are clean.

547
00:24:59,698 --> 00:25:00,832
Oh, you're right.

548
00:25:02,934 --> 00:25:05,337
It's nice that it’s got a dryer.

549
00:25:05,403 --> 00:25:06,705
Isn't that the best?

550
00:25:07,372 --> 00:25:10,008
The kitchen faces the entrance,

551
00:25:10,075 --> 00:25:11,443
so you may find it a bit cramped.

552
00:25:12,043 --> 00:25:13,011
Well…

553
00:25:13,078 --> 00:25:15,347
I mostly eat out, so it's totally fine.

554
00:25:15,413 --> 00:25:17,749
Yeah, no problem at all.

555
00:25:17,816 --> 00:25:18,884
That's great to hear.

556
00:25:24,322 --> 00:25:26,925
This is apparently
the landlord’s favorite color.

557
00:25:27,826 --> 00:25:29,461
It's quite unique, to say the least.

558
00:25:29,528 --> 00:25:31,730
Yeah, a little, isn’t it?

559
00:25:31,796 --> 00:25:33,565
That’s a nice color!

560
00:25:33,632 --> 00:25:34,866
Yeah, yeah, really nice.

561
00:25:34,933 --> 00:25:35,800
Which is it?

562
00:25:40,605 --> 00:25:42,674
I think it’s very cute.

563
00:25:43,275 --> 00:25:46,578
I find it a bit unsettling.

564
00:25:46,645 --> 00:25:47,746
Right.

565
00:25:48,346 --> 00:25:51,917
The room in the back
is the only one that has tatami flooring.

566
00:25:53,184 --> 00:25:54,486
Oh, tatami!

567
00:25:54,553 --> 00:25:56,254
Ah, sorry.

568
00:25:56,321 --> 00:25:57,822
- One moment.
- Sure.

569
00:26:02,427 --> 00:26:03,628
Tatami, huh?

570
00:26:04,162 --> 00:26:05,897
Isn't tatami nice?

571
00:26:07,365 --> 00:26:08,900
My parents' home had tatami flooring.

572
00:26:09,935 --> 00:26:11,202
Back then,

573
00:26:11,269 --> 00:26:14,606
I envied my friends'
shiny hardwood floors,

574
00:26:14,673 --> 00:26:15,774
but in the end,

575
00:26:15,840 --> 00:26:18,810
it’s just so comforting.
The smell and all.

576
00:26:18,877 --> 00:26:19,778
Is it a detached house?

577
00:26:19,844 --> 00:26:20,979
Yep.

578
00:26:21,513 --> 00:26:23,548
- Was it a "clamp"?
- What?

579
00:26:23,615 --> 00:26:26,818
I was wondering if using the house
as a clamp actually worked.

580
00:26:27,619 --> 00:26:29,721
My dad and mom are still together.

581
00:26:29,788 --> 00:26:32,424
Whether it’s thanks to the house,
I’m not sure, though.

582
00:26:32,490 --> 00:26:33,558
Okay.

583
00:26:33,625 --> 00:26:36,695
What was your parents' home like, Sakuta?

584
00:26:39,064 --> 00:26:41,933
It had lots of rooms.
I guess it was a lively place.

585
00:26:42,767 --> 00:26:44,302
Oh, so you had, like, a big family?

586
00:26:44,369 --> 00:26:46,037
No, I grew up in a facility.

587
00:26:46,104 --> 00:26:48,106
I didn't have parents
ever since I was born.

588
00:26:48,974 --> 00:26:50,542
I was raised in a nursery,

589
00:26:50,609 --> 00:26:52,644
then I went straight to an orphanage.

590
00:26:53,878 --> 00:26:55,080
It was fun.

591
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:58,316
I had many close friends,

592
00:26:59,117 --> 00:27:00,852
and the food was amazing.

593
00:27:01,853 --> 00:27:02,854
Um…

594
00:27:04,089 --> 00:27:05,323
You've been through a lot, huh?

595
00:27:05,390 --> 00:27:06,524
Not really.

596
00:27:07,258 --> 00:27:08,660
Everyone's been through stuff, no?

597
00:27:09,494 --> 00:27:11,830
Hotaru, and even you, Hatano.

598
00:27:12,664 --> 00:27:14,032
My situation is nothing special.

599
00:27:14,766 --> 00:27:16,868
Me? I didn't really…

600
00:27:21,306 --> 00:27:22,240
What's the matter?

601
00:27:23,508 --> 00:27:25,944
There's people flirting out there.

602
00:27:27,912 --> 00:27:30,715
If we can see their flirting from here,

603
00:27:30,782 --> 00:27:33,118
that means the flirting on this side

604
00:27:33,184 --> 00:27:34,986
can be seen by them too, right?

605
00:27:35,053 --> 00:27:38,089
What, do you have plans to flirt?

606
00:27:43,828 --> 00:27:45,897
I wonder how we look
from their point of view.

607
00:27:46,898 --> 00:27:47,732
Huh?

608
00:27:47,799 --> 00:27:48,933
The two of us.

609
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:50,335
Even earlier,

610
00:27:50,402 --> 00:27:52,737
we were mistaken for siblings and friends.

611
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:57,776
If a guy and a girl are together,
people just assume

612
00:27:57,842 --> 00:27:59,811
they’re a couple, right?

613
00:28:00,378 --> 00:28:02,547
So, why is it different for two guys?

614
00:28:02,614 --> 00:28:04,849
But we’re not actually dating.

615
00:28:05,817 --> 00:28:07,852
Well, yeah. That’s true,

616
00:28:07,919 --> 00:28:11,389
but I can’t help feeling a little jealous.

617
00:28:18,329 --> 00:28:19,864
The door color…

618
00:28:19,931 --> 00:28:22,701
It's starting to look kind of cute now.

619
00:28:29,941 --> 00:28:32,477
Sorry for the wait. How’s it looking?

620
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:35,146
- Oh, sorry. I wanted to ask…
- Yes?

621
00:28:35,213 --> 00:28:38,783
About the security deposit…

622
00:28:42,287 --> 00:28:45,523
HIGH SCHOOL PAMPHLET

623
00:29:01,973 --> 00:29:03,308
- Hey.
- What the?

624
00:29:03,374 --> 00:29:04,642
Can I come in for a sec?

625
00:29:04,709 --> 00:29:05,577
No.

626
00:29:05,643 --> 00:29:08,213
I just want to check if the money
is in there or not.

627
00:29:08,279 --> 00:29:09,114
Please leave.

628
00:29:09,180 --> 00:29:10,715
Come on. It'll be quick.

629
00:29:11,683 --> 00:29:13,518
- Leave!
- Be quiet.

630
00:29:13,585 --> 00:29:15,854
- Leave!
- Hey, let me in, will you?

631
00:29:15,920 --> 00:29:17,021
- Come on!
- No!

632
00:29:17,088 --> 00:29:18,423
Hey, you! What are you doing?

633
00:29:19,457 --> 00:29:21,226
No, it's nothing.

634
00:29:21,292 --> 00:29:23,728
Use the man catcher, Kusunoki!
The one I gave you!

635
00:29:23,795 --> 00:29:25,697
You're misunderstanding.
Don't raise your voice.

636
00:29:25,764 --> 00:29:27,398
It's really nothing.

637
00:29:28,166 --> 00:29:29,200
Hey, that's dangerous!

638
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:30,735
What's wrong with you?

639
00:29:31,269 --> 00:29:32,804
Hey, it's dangerous!

640
00:29:34,572 --> 00:29:35,907
And what's with those cries?

641
00:29:35,974 --> 00:29:37,208
Stop shouting!

642
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:39,444
Hey! Stop! Ouch!

643
00:29:39,511 --> 00:29:41,479
- Am I doing it right?
- Ouch!

644
00:29:41,546 --> 00:29:43,615
Yes! What should I do?

645
00:29:43,681 --> 00:29:45,950
Stop going for my shank!

646
00:29:46,017 --> 00:29:46,985
What's your deal?

647
00:29:47,786 --> 00:29:50,288
Will you be looking at other places too?

648
00:29:50,355 --> 00:29:52,090
I'd like to decide
after seeing a few more.

649
00:29:52,757 --> 00:29:53,758
Sounds good.

650
00:29:53,825 --> 00:29:55,260
- What should I do…?
- Huh?

651
00:29:56,227 --> 00:29:58,797
- What's wrong?
- Come with me, quick!

652
00:29:59,664 --> 00:30:00,632
Okay.

653
00:30:03,234 --> 00:30:05,970
Why are you like this?
I'll leave after seeing it for myself.

654
00:30:06,037 --> 00:30:07,806
This is Mom’s and my home!

655
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:11,643
You're hiding it, right? Give me the key.

656
00:30:11,709 --> 00:30:13,378
- Hey!
- Coming through!

657
00:30:13,444 --> 00:30:15,313
- Excuse me! Coming through!
- Hey!

658
00:30:15,380 --> 00:30:16,581
Stop this!

659
00:30:17,849 --> 00:30:19,484
- Hey!
- What's this?

660
00:30:24,923 --> 00:30:26,858
- The key.
- What?

661
00:30:26,925 --> 00:30:28,660
Just pass me the key!

662
00:30:31,429 --> 00:30:32,730
Come on.

663
00:30:32,797 --> 00:30:33,998
Leave.

664
00:30:34,065 --> 00:30:36,201
- What's going on?
- He's a suspicious person.

665
00:30:36,267 --> 00:30:37,569
- Who're you calling that!
- Hey, now.

666
00:30:38,169 --> 00:30:39,370
What now?

667
00:30:39,437 --> 00:30:41,773
Um… Who may you be?

668
00:30:44,943 --> 00:30:46,144
I'm her dad. Why?

669
00:30:47,912 --> 00:30:49,280
- What?
- Oh my.

670
00:30:50,248 --> 00:30:52,383
You know her mom's case, right?

671
00:30:53,351 --> 00:30:54,219
Well…

672
00:30:55,086 --> 00:30:56,120
‪Yeah.

673
00:30:56,187 --> 00:30:57,989
I’m looking for the stolen money.

674
00:30:59,023 --> 00:31:00,525
If she’s hiding it,

675
00:31:01,092 --> 00:31:02,794
I’ll need to report it to the police.

676
00:31:03,494 --> 00:31:05,096
And I’m worried about her.

677
00:31:06,097 --> 00:31:09,133
Sorry for the ruckus.
This is a private family matter.

678
00:31:09,200 --> 00:31:10,969
You all can leave now.
And remove this too.

679
00:31:13,438 --> 00:31:14,339
Then,

680
00:31:15,139 --> 00:31:16,608
why didn’t you come until now?

681
00:31:17,242 --> 00:31:18,076
What?

682
00:31:18,610 --> 00:31:21,579
- You're just her neighbor, right?
- No.

683
00:31:22,280 --> 00:31:24,682
Are you perhaps
from the child guidance center?

684
00:31:24,749 --> 00:31:25,884
No.

685
00:31:25,950 --> 00:31:27,752
Oh, then you must be her teacher.

686
00:31:27,819 --> 00:31:29,854
Ah, that'd be me.

687
00:31:29,921 --> 00:31:30,755
Right.

688
00:31:30,822 --> 00:31:31,990
Then, you're the landlord?

689
00:31:32,056 --> 00:31:33,124
That'd be me.

690
00:31:33,191 --> 00:31:34,926
Okay. Then…

691
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:40,698
I'm her dad.

692
00:31:42,567 --> 00:31:43,701
Huh?

693
00:31:45,303 --> 00:31:46,437
I'm her dad!

694
00:31:47,305 --> 00:31:48,139
Huh?

695
00:31:50,508 --> 00:31:52,377
He's my new dad.

696
00:31:52,443 --> 00:31:54,679
She's right. He's her dad.

697
00:31:54,746 --> 00:31:56,447
Nice to meet you. I'm her dad.

698
00:31:58,082 --> 00:31:59,851
What kind of crap are you pulling?

699
00:32:01,853 --> 00:32:04,722
- I mean, you're gay, no?
- Hey!

700
00:32:06,190 --> 00:32:08,126
A gay person calling himself
a dad is weird.

701
00:32:08,192 --> 00:32:09,227
Come on!

702
00:32:09,294 --> 00:32:11,596
- It's not weird at all!
- Huh?

703
00:32:11,663 --> 00:32:13,932
What’s wrong with a gay dad?

704
00:32:13,998 --> 00:32:15,233
- Am I right?
- Yes.

705
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:17,635
It's not weird. It's awesome.

706
00:32:18,636 --> 00:32:20,805
Look, we’re blood-related here.

707
00:32:21,306 --> 00:32:23,675
Well, I’ve been
to a parent-teacher conference,

708
00:32:23,741 --> 00:32:25,643
spoken to the police,

709
00:32:26,177 --> 00:32:28,179
eaten ice cream together, shared shishamo,

710
00:32:28,246 --> 00:32:29,914
miso soup and rice balls…

711
00:32:31,249 --> 00:32:32,583
Whether to scold her or not,

712
00:32:32,650 --> 00:32:34,252
I wondered about that,
and I worried for her.

713
00:32:35,586 --> 00:32:37,422
I've been told I didn’t have to do that,

714
00:32:37,488 --> 00:32:38,856
so what does that make me?

715
00:32:39,557 --> 00:32:40,558
Nothing, duh.

716
00:32:40,625 --> 00:32:42,927
I'm the one who seems
more like a parent, no?

717
00:32:42,994 --> 00:32:44,162
Yes, you very much do!

718
00:32:44,228 --> 00:32:45,229
Isn't that right?

719
00:32:45,863 --> 00:32:47,065
What?

720
00:32:47,131 --> 00:32:49,300
That's not the point here.

721
00:32:49,367 --> 00:32:51,970
Then what is?
This kind of stuff matters, right?

722
00:32:53,171 --> 00:32:55,473
So, you’re after the 30 million too?

723
00:32:55,540 --> 00:32:56,641
Too?

724
00:32:56,708 --> 00:32:59,143
You guys are in on it too?

725
00:32:59,911 --> 00:33:01,612
Planning to split it all, huh?

726
00:33:01,679 --> 00:33:03,481
That's not it.

727
00:33:03,548 --> 00:33:05,984
Then what's the deal?
You’re a teacher, right?

728
00:33:06,050 --> 00:33:07,785
You're letting this guy do what he wants?

729
00:33:10,321 --> 00:33:12,757
Okay, I'm calling the police.

730
00:33:12,824 --> 00:33:13,691
Huh?

731
00:33:14,325 --> 00:33:15,393
- What?
- Um…

732
00:33:16,561 --> 00:33:18,229
Wait, please!

733
00:33:23,134 --> 00:33:24,035
Fine.

734
00:33:24,535 --> 00:33:27,138
Give me the key,
and I won’t call the police.

735
00:33:32,777 --> 00:33:33,644
Huh?

736
00:33:34,178 --> 00:33:37,281
Whatever. Look as much as you want.

737
00:33:37,348 --> 00:33:38,182
But…

738
00:33:38,816 --> 00:33:40,351
It's for your sake, Dad.

739
00:33:40,418 --> 00:33:42,520
- What did I say?
- I'm not referring to you.

740
00:33:43,121 --> 00:33:44,355
It's him I'm talking about.

741
00:33:46,157 --> 00:33:47,258
Is that so?

742
00:33:53,731 --> 00:33:54,565
Will it be alright?

743
00:33:54,632 --> 00:33:55,800
Sorry about this.

744
00:33:56,334 --> 00:33:57,268
You sure about this?

745
00:33:57,835 --> 00:34:00,304
There’s no money in my unit anyway.

746
00:34:02,774 --> 00:34:05,009
In other words, it's somewhere else?

747
00:34:05,076 --> 00:34:06,277
Is that true?

748
00:34:06,844 --> 00:34:09,947
So, that person earlier was Jin Ichigaya?

749
00:34:12,984 --> 00:34:14,952
You’ve been lying all this time?

750
00:34:17,054 --> 00:34:18,489
Can both of you

751
00:34:19,257 --> 00:34:23,194
give me some explanation?

752
00:34:48,119 --> 00:34:49,720
What the hell?

753
00:34:55,359 --> 00:34:57,295
CHASU

754
00:34:57,361 --> 00:34:59,230
CHAN

755
00:35:02,133 --> 00:35:03,167
What do I do with this?

756
00:35:04,302 --> 00:35:06,504
PARTY A: HOTARU KUSUNOKI
PARTY B: GENICHI HATANO

757
00:35:06,571 --> 00:35:07,638
PARENT-CHILD CONTRACT

758
00:35:07,705 --> 00:35:09,941
Parent-Child Contract?

759
00:35:10,007 --> 00:35:12,310
Landlady, were you aware of this too?

760
00:35:14,779 --> 00:35:16,714
Yeah. About pretending to be her parent.

761
00:35:17,348 --> 00:35:18,683
The 30 million yen though…

762
00:35:19,650 --> 00:35:20,551
surprised me.

763
00:35:32,163 --> 00:35:33,297
Dang it!

764
00:35:33,364 --> 00:35:35,299
BANKBOOK

765
00:35:38,903 --> 00:35:40,171
Found nothing, right?

766
00:35:40,738 --> 00:35:42,373
Please don’t ever come back again.

767
00:35:44,142 --> 00:35:45,343
Remember, I'm your dad.

768
00:35:46,644 --> 00:35:48,012
Are you hungry, by any chance?

769
00:35:48,079 --> 00:35:48,946
Huh?

770
00:35:49,013 --> 00:35:52,116
Hunger can make you do bad things.
Like crows.

771
00:35:52,750 --> 00:35:54,218
Don’t compare me to them!

772
00:35:55,887 --> 00:35:56,988
Bye!

773
00:36:01,959 --> 00:36:04,028
- Has your dad left?
- Yes.

774
00:36:07,865 --> 00:36:09,800
What, the cash is in there?

775
00:36:15,673 --> 00:36:16,707
Well…

776
00:36:16,774 --> 00:36:19,043
It's not really what I expected.

777
00:36:19,110 --> 00:36:20,578
I imagined gold coins.

778
00:36:21,379 --> 00:36:23,981
Okay, you can put that away now.

779
00:36:24,048 --> 00:36:25,249
Okay.

780
00:36:28,152 --> 00:36:29,353
The man catcher…

781
00:36:29,987 --> 00:36:32,056
I'll prepare more of them.

782
00:36:32,857 --> 00:36:33,958
Have a good rest.

783
00:36:45,403 --> 00:36:46,237
Here.

784
00:36:50,908 --> 00:36:52,343
Sorry about this.

785
00:36:53,711 --> 00:36:56,214
- What?
- I made you lie.

786
00:36:56,948 --> 00:36:59,217
It's not really your fault.

787
00:37:00,651 --> 00:37:02,954
I don’t have parents,

788
00:37:03,020 --> 00:37:04,522
and I like guys.

789
00:37:04,589 --> 00:37:05,623
Huh?

790
00:37:05,690 --> 00:37:08,259
I used to make up fake parents
and fake girlfriends

791
00:37:08,326 --> 00:37:09,894
and tell my friends about them.

792
00:37:10,394 --> 00:37:13,231
Then, it got exhausting.

793
00:37:14,599 --> 00:37:17,902
I even kept a notebook
to keep my lies consistent.

794
00:37:19,870 --> 00:37:20,738
But…

795
00:37:21,706 --> 00:37:25,243
I lost track of what I said to who,
and everything started falling apart.

796
00:37:25,810 --> 00:37:27,678
So, I just stopped hiding it.

797
00:37:28,746 --> 00:37:30,815
But at school…

798
00:37:31,649 --> 00:37:33,251
no one knows, right?

799
00:37:34,051 --> 00:37:37,421
I’m not hiding it,
I just choose who I tell.

800
00:37:38,856 --> 00:37:39,757
I see.

801
00:37:41,359 --> 00:37:43,327
So, I'm sorry.

802
00:37:44,929 --> 00:37:47,064
I get how hard it is
to keep up appearances.

803
00:37:48,332 --> 00:37:50,134
So, Mr. Hatano knows too?

804
00:37:50,901 --> 00:37:52,703
Yeah.

805
00:37:54,939 --> 00:37:57,475
Why did you ask for Hatano's help?

806
00:37:57,541 --> 00:37:58,376
Huh?

807
00:37:59,243 --> 00:38:00,945
Is it because he lives here too?

808
00:38:03,247 --> 00:38:05,316
Or is it because he's gay?

809
00:38:09,920 --> 00:38:11,789
I thought he's similar.

810
00:38:12,523 --> 00:38:13,457
What do you mean?

811
00:38:14,258 --> 00:38:15,326
His looks?

812
00:38:19,263 --> 00:38:20,564
How he's doing his best.

813
00:38:32,677 --> 00:38:35,846
Mr. Sakuta said he's got the gist of it,
so he'll think it over.

814
00:38:36,547 --> 00:38:37,548
Think what over?

815
00:38:39,016 --> 00:38:41,652
I also heard he didn't have parents
and that he's gay.

816
00:38:42,853 --> 00:38:44,855
- From Sakuta?
- Yes.

817
00:38:47,758 --> 00:38:50,227
Right, dinner.

818
00:38:51,095 --> 00:38:53,597
The cat's already out of the bag,
so I'm returning to my unit.

819
00:38:53,664 --> 00:38:54,732
Oh, okay.

820
00:38:57,535 --> 00:38:58,869
But…

821
00:39:00,638 --> 00:39:02,440
- As my current dad,
- Yes?

822
00:39:02,506 --> 00:39:04,108
I've got a favor to ask of you.

823
00:39:07,278 --> 00:39:08,312
Welcome.

824
00:39:08,379 --> 00:39:09,113
TRUE MIRIN

825
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:10,014
Here.

826
00:39:12,650 --> 00:39:14,085
I’m with my dad today.

827
00:39:17,488 --> 00:39:18,322
Hi.

828
00:39:21,926 --> 00:39:23,227
451 yen, please.

829
00:39:23,294 --> 00:39:24,628
Glad you could buy it!

830
00:39:24,695 --> 00:39:26,497
You did it!

831
00:39:26,564 --> 00:39:30,201
Yay!

832
00:39:30,267 --> 00:39:32,069
Though, that's a little unfair.

833
00:39:32,136 --> 00:39:33,270
COFFEE TO GO

834
00:39:33,337 --> 00:39:35,106
We'll be going first.

835
00:39:35,172 --> 00:39:37,074
Having a parent is convenient after all.

836
00:39:37,141 --> 00:39:39,243
How nice to be you.
It does seem convenient.

837
00:39:39,910 --> 00:39:41,779
Can you pretend to be my dad too?

838
00:39:41,846 --> 00:39:42,780
What?

839
00:39:42,847 --> 00:39:44,448
I'm just joking.

840
00:39:45,649 --> 00:39:47,151
Hey, you don't have a dad?

841
00:39:48,319 --> 00:39:50,688
I do, but it's, like, better
if he’s not around.

842
00:39:52,490 --> 00:39:53,557
Wanna keep playing?

843
00:39:54,325 --> 00:39:56,127
Nah. I’m heading home. See you.

844
00:39:57,595 --> 00:40:00,197
TRUE MIRIN

845
00:40:01,031 --> 00:40:03,834
Hey, is that your mom’s secret ingredient?

846
00:40:04,568 --> 00:40:06,170
Yes, that's right.

847
00:40:06,771 --> 00:40:08,539
Hey, are you always hanging out here?

848
00:40:09,940 --> 00:40:11,208
This place is awful, isn’t it?

849
00:40:11,709 --> 00:40:12,576
Huh?

850
00:40:12,643 --> 00:40:14,612
It's dirty and scary.

851
00:40:15,913 --> 00:40:17,248
But somehow, it mattered to me.

852
00:40:17,882 --> 00:40:20,384
I kept wondering why.

853
00:40:20,451 --> 00:40:21,352
Uh-huh.

854
00:40:21,419 --> 00:40:23,187
And maybe it's because I chose it myself.

855
00:40:28,759 --> 00:40:29,660
I see.

856
00:40:35,699 --> 00:40:38,302
TRUE MIRIN

857
00:40:44,074 --> 00:40:46,076
After the beep tone,

858
00:40:46,143 --> 00:40:48,846
please leave your name and message.

859
00:40:49,547 --> 00:40:51,048
Hello, Mom?

860
00:40:51,782 --> 00:40:54,485
I need to start deciding on my future.

861
00:40:54,552 --> 00:40:56,387
Like, which high school to go to.

862
00:40:57,455 --> 00:40:59,290
Choosing is hard, isn't it?

863
00:40:59,356 --> 00:41:01,258
Even stuff like what goes in my rice ball

864
00:41:01,325 --> 00:41:03,661
or who I tell my secrets to.

865
00:41:03,727 --> 00:41:05,162
It’s really tough.

866
00:41:06,096 --> 00:41:07,331
Coming.

867
00:41:07,398 --> 00:41:08,566
- But…
- Yes?

868
00:41:08,632 --> 00:41:10,134
I’ll do my best to choose carefully.

869
00:41:11,735 --> 00:41:14,438
So I can take care
of everything around me.

870
00:41:16,173 --> 00:41:18,476
Starting with
today’s miso soup ingredients.

871
00:41:21,011 --> 00:41:22,813
Talk to you soon. Bye.

872
00:41:24,515 --> 00:41:25,749
Let's taste test!

873
00:41:36,494 --> 00:41:37,895
‪YAMANASHI GRAPE JUICE, OKAYAMA GRAPE JUICE

874
00:41:37,962 --> 00:41:38,863
It's a draw.

875
00:41:47,004 --> 00:41:48,739
Excuse me!

876
00:41:48,806 --> 00:41:49,707
Yes?

877
00:41:49,773 --> 00:41:51,609
Sorry.

878
00:41:51,675 --> 00:41:52,576
Uh…

879
00:41:53,177 --> 00:41:54,812
The day before yesterday,

880
00:41:54,879 --> 00:41:58,682
or maybe the day before that, I think,
I sent a letter to Tokyo.

881
00:41:58,749 --> 00:42:00,651
- Right.
- Has it arrived by any chance?

882
00:42:00,718 --> 00:42:03,621
Normally, it should be there by now.

883
00:42:04,488 --> 00:42:05,322
Is that right?

884
00:42:05,389 --> 00:42:07,258
Did you send it out by mistake, perhaps?

885
00:42:07,324 --> 00:42:08,225
Why do you ask?

886
00:42:08,292 --> 00:42:09,994
You sound like you wished
it wasn't sent out.

887
00:42:10,060 --> 00:42:12,229
Ah, no…

888
00:42:12,296 --> 00:42:12,963
‪TAMOTSU’S LITTLE GIFT SHOP

889
00:42:13,030 --> 00:42:13,864
I’m not sure.

890
00:42:15,432 --> 00:42:16,867
Maybe I did send it to the wrong place.

891
00:42:19,203 --> 00:42:21,572
I honestly don’t know myself too.

892
00:42:26,143 --> 00:42:27,845
- I thought about it,
- Uh-huh.

893
00:42:28,412 --> 00:42:31,315
and honestly, I don’t know what to do.

894
00:42:31,382 --> 00:42:32,516
Right.

895
00:42:32,583 --> 00:42:34,385
Why did you pretend to be her parent?

896
00:42:34,451 --> 00:42:35,452
Huh?

897
00:42:36,020 --> 00:42:39,690
I mean, there are the police,
the child guidance center, and so on.

898
00:42:39,757 --> 00:42:42,159
There are many places out there
to support Hotaru.

899
00:42:42,760 --> 00:42:46,697
And yet, you still went out of your way
to act as her dad.

900
00:42:46,764 --> 00:42:48,065
I really don’t get it.

901
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:52,036
Are you in it for the money?

902
00:42:52,102 --> 00:42:53,771
- What?
- The 30 million yen.

903
00:42:53,837 --> 00:42:56,307
Oh, not at all. I don't know if that money

904
00:42:56,373 --> 00:42:57,508
was from embezzlement, but…

905
00:42:57,575 --> 00:42:59,443
I'm sure it's meant for Hotaru.

906
00:43:01,145 --> 00:43:02,246
Then…

907
00:43:03,080 --> 00:43:05,249
is there another reason?

908
00:43:05,983 --> 00:43:08,419
Because I was asked to pretend
to be her parent.

909
00:43:09,019 --> 00:43:11,088
Do you do everything someone asks?

910
00:43:12,289 --> 00:43:13,123
She was in a fix.

911
00:43:13,891 --> 00:43:16,060
- Are you always like this?
- What?

912
00:43:16,126 --> 00:43:17,962
This is not the first time
this has happened.

913
00:43:18,028 --> 00:43:19,530
Whether it's using a house as a clamp,

914
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:21,332
introducing me to this place,

915
00:43:21,398 --> 00:43:22,366
or finding an apartment--

916
00:43:22,433 --> 00:43:24,835
That's… different.

917
00:43:24,902 --> 00:43:25,803
How so?

918
00:43:28,839 --> 00:43:31,141
That's because I was worried.

919
00:43:32,643 --> 00:43:36,213
Yeah, because I was in a fix, right?

920
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:37,114
Oh, no.

921
00:43:37,781 --> 00:43:39,683
That's not exactly it.

922
00:43:39,750 --> 00:43:40,951
Then, what is it?

923
00:43:43,754 --> 00:43:44,655
Look…

924
00:43:45,356 --> 00:43:46,790
I won't know if you don't tell.

925
00:43:48,792 --> 00:43:50,194
I like you.

926
00:43:52,429 --> 00:43:53,697
Sorry, what?

927
00:43:53,764 --> 00:43:54,765
I said…

928
00:43:57,067 --> 00:43:58,135
I like you!

929
00:44:03,407 --> 00:44:04,274
Huh?

930
00:44:04,775 --> 00:44:07,344
INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

931
00:45:48,979 --> 00:45:51,482
Subtitle translation by: Jeffery
